# Frozen population for the catalog-wide robustness check (report section 06).
# Real TLEs fetched from Celestrak (celestrak.org) 2026-08-06, one snapshot.
#
# HOW THESE 41 OBJECTS WERE CHOSEN (deterministic rule, not hand-picked):
#   From ~1000 objects across 13 Celestrak groups + a few named eccentric
#   satellites, we kept EVERY object with e>0.1 (the cases that stress the
#   bound), then sampled near-circular objects evenly by period within each of
#   5 period bands (LEO..deep-space). Goal: span orbit period and, above all,
#   eccentricity (e = 0.0002 to 0.91) -- diversity, not raw count.
# Frozen here so the analysis is exactly reproducible without re-pulling a live
# catalog (TLE epochs drift daily). Format: name, line1, line2.
